    <section class="section" id="ladder">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>3. Ladder Diagram</h2>
        <p class="body">
          The ladder editor draws rungs, and the PLC panel's text view shows the same rungs in a text form. IEC gives
          ladder no text form, so this one is the project's own. A rung is translated to Structured Text and run by the
          same engine, so everything in section 2 is available to a ladder program, and the export writes a ladder POU
          as a PLCopen LD body.
        </p>
        <h3>The text form</h3>
        <div class="scroll-x">
          <table class="elements">
            <thead><tr><th>Text</th><th>Element</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              ${LD_ELEMENTS.map(([t, what]) => `<tr><td class="m" translate="no">${esc(t)}</td><td>${esc(what)}</td></tr>`).join('\n              ')}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        ${cards(pick(ladder, 'supported'), false)}
        <h3>How rungs run</h3>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>A rung runs left to right, each element once, and each element sees what the elements before it wrote. Rungs run top to bottom.</li>
          <li>IEC leaves the order of a branch's paths open. Paths that hold a contact or a block run first, then paths that hold only coils, each group top to bottom. So a contact on one path of a branch reads a variable as it was before a coil-only path of the same branch writes it.</li>
          <li>An edge contact passes power for one evaluation after its variable rose or fell. Its memory is updated every evaluation, even while the rung is off, and starts FALSE.</li>
          <li>A box behind EN is not called while the rung is off. Its outputs hold their values and ENO is off.</li>
          <li>While a jump's rung is on, the rungs between it and its label are not evaluated, so their coils hold what they last wrote. Jumps go down the section only.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Not supported</h3>
        ${refusals(pick(ladder, 'unsupported'), false)}
        <h3>Valid IEC, with an export caveat</h3>
        <p class="sub">
          These are valid IEC ladder and run here. Some targets' importers may not accept them, so the PLCopen export
          warns about each.
        </p>
        ${caveats(pick(ladder, 'permissive'))}
      </div>
    </section>

